  <section|Exact World producer><label|exact-world-producer>

  The source theorem is <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.World.overlap> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/RG08/Flat/World.lean>. Its hypotheses are:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|World.Provides H P>: for every world point <verbatim|x>,
    its horizon satisfies <verbatim|Suffices P>; for every <verbatim|low x
    \<leq\> i \<less\> fine x>, the actual order-two tower at cutoff
    <verbatim|fine x>, level <verbatim|i>, has the same coefficient kernel as
    the Wilson flight-duo tower for that schedule and penalty.

    <item><verbatim|World.Funding W P w \<theta\>>: a common positive width
    <verbatim|w>, bounded by the map width <verbatim|\<alpha\>>; adjacent
    widths fit both prices; <verbatim|\<theta\>\<gtr\>0>; each adjacent fold
    satisfies <verbatim|2*w_i \<leq\> L_i*w_{i+1}>; the exact
    <verbatim|neutralCoin> charge at width <verbatim|w_{i+1}> is at most the
    staircase drop; and the top allowance is a polynomial in the prescribed
    age.
  </enumerate>

  Its conclusion constructs one packet for each <verbatim|(x,i)> in the world
  interval, with folded cost bounded by <verbatim|A * age(x,i)^d * (a(fine
  x)/a(i))^c>, for uniform <verbatim|A\<geq\>0>, <verbatim|d\<in\>\<bbb-N\>>,
  and <verbatim|c\<gtr\>0>. The packet is neutral, unit-lattice covariant,
  and represents the quadratic-precision difference on every torus side
  tested by the world. The article expands the private helpers
  <verbatim|at_end>, <verbatim|to_here>, and <verbatim|existsRows> instead of
  identifying the result with record unpacking.

