  packages the world points as <verbatim|(measure k, cutoff N, later history
  n)> and calls <verbatim|World.overlap>; it then resolves the resulting
  curvature packet using the two metric row strips.>>>>>

  <section|Selected public route><label|selected-public-route>

  The world producer is reached through the actual selected construction, not
  a neighboring proof interface:

  <\enumerate>
    <item><verbatim|YM.Independent.constructionRun> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/Independent/ConstructionRun.lean> calls
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.R2I.RG05Joint.selectRunWithTreasuryPeriod_preselected_quote_orders_postnumeric>.

    <item>Its <verbatim|Choice> is <verbatim|YM.Integration.NativeComponentRecipe.Choice>;
    the nonempty choice comes from <verbatim|NativeComponentRecipe.available>,
    whose flat supplier is the result of <verbatim|YM.RG08.Flat.entrance_gate>.

    <item><verbatim|NativeComponentRecipe.realize> applies that supplier to
    the selected schedule and a horizon with the required <verbatim|Suffices>
    bounds. The binding to the original run is
    <verbatim|YM.Integration.ActualRunNativeComponentRecipe.on_run> and
    <verbatim|.of_preselection>; it uses the original
    <verbatim|R.family.path.levels> and <verbatim|R.alloy.B.M>.

    <item>The public same-witness extraction route also uses
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Run.again>, whose proof calls the
    actual full-volume <verbatim|ahead> supplier and retains its same-run
    data. This is the route containing the <verbatim|Ahead>/garden/Mauve
    chain; no nearby Cook/Multi interface is substituted here.

    <item>The <verbatim|Volant> step used by the retained step story is
    supplied by <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.paneer> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Wax.lean>. Its local constructor is
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Many.ripe> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tanger.lean>; that proof calls
    <verbatim|Photo.bidding>, <verbatim|Many.usable>, <verbatim|Many.crowd2>,
    and <verbatim|Photo.shade>. In the selected tower story,
    <verbatim|Bandage.escape> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stove.lean>
    turns the step suppliers into the <verbatim|Moonlit> data consumed by
    <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.ahead> in
    <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Forge.lean>.
  </enumerate>

  <section|Volant source correspondence><label|volant-source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Article
  step>>|<cell|<strong|Exact declaration/path>>|<cell|<strong|Source content
  inspected>>>|<row|<cell|shipment tariff>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Palette.shipPrice>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Permit.lean>>|<cell|<math|N<space|0.17em><math-up|siteFactor><around|(|<math-up|radiusB><around|(|x|)>|)>*exp
  <around|(|<around|(|Q.*r*e*l*a*t*i*v*e+1|)><math-up|preCost><around|(|Q.*h*a*l*o+5|)>|)>*a\<leqslant\><math-up|ribbon><around|(|Q,L,x|)>>.>>|<row|<cell|offer
  and support to menu plot>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Merge.Photo.bidding>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tinder.lean>>|<cell|Uses the offer's
  site/budget fields, occupied parent sites, threshold
  <verbatim|4\<leq\>relative>, exponent <verbatim|100\<leq\>supportExponent>,
  and the ship-price inequality to apply the rooted budget
  theorem.>>|<row|<cell|rooted tariff conversion>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.root_hit>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Root.lean>>|<cell|Given per-site
  occupancy <verbatim|N>, a rooted budget at exponent <verbatim|relative+1>,
  and one named origin in each positive mode whose image lies in its birth
  support, returns the hit ledger at exponent <verbatim|relative> with budget
  <verbatim|N*siteFactor(B0)*c>; the lost cover exponent is
  exact.>>|<row|<cell|finite menu payments>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Many.usable>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stage.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|Palette.fair>
  supplies paid trained terms at the product fee <verbatim|lace>;
  <verbatim|Palette.sizes> applies <verbatim|Charity.everyoneN> to prove
  summability; <verbatim|Palette.lucent> gives the rooted fee bound, then
  scaling by two yields <verbatim|2*pledgeA/(1-sailUp)>; the source
  identifies exponent <verbatim|earn+w>; <verbatim|crowd>,
  <verbatim|listens>, and <verbatim|valueP> give the gas response, locality,
  and exact closed push identity.>>|<row|<cell|second response-cost
  payment>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Mallow.Many.crowd2>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Paprika.lean>>|<cell|Uses the second
  <verbatim|Arrives> clause for the exact <verbatim|softNeed> request and
  <verbatim|within_alpha>; <verbatim|plants> obtains <verbatim|Vapor> from
  <verbatim|Mallow.cools>; <verbatim|corps2> uses the first rate clause to
  pay the precursor at <verbatim|stems>; <verbatim|Motion.widening> and
  <verbatim|Motion.harvest> transport the selected rates through finalization
  to a <verbatim|Pays> bound at <verbatim|straw>.>>|<row|<cell|polynomial
  assembly to a canopy>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Merge.Photo.shade>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Shaded.lean>>|<cell|Chooses signed single-menu
  polynomials, assembles the field-mode polynomial, and proves its ledgers
  using the paid menu and response bounds, support localization, and the
  supplied exact jet equality. Its helpers are <verbatim|exquisite>,
  <verbatim|serenade>, <verbatim|excavation>, <verbatim|heavily>,
  <verbatim|selfie>, and <verbatim|scored> in
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Magma.lean>; the latter expands the push as
  the exponential factor times <verbatim|pass(sum spine)> times the field
  polynomial of the field-mode tally.>>|<row|<cell|full one-step
  witness>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Menu.Volant>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Copse.lean>>|<cell|Reserves are precisely the
  canopy statement; the other fields are propagation, tuning, and the
  slot-separation arsenal. <verbatim|Many.ripe> supplies them from
  <verbatim|sounds>, <verbatim|tunes>, and <verbatim|sharp> after
  constructing the canopy.>>>>>

  The revised <verbatim|rg-construction.tex> records the shipment arithmetic
  and a conditional fiberwise assembly from ungrouped paid terms. The new
  <verbatim|rg-multisource.tex> expands <verbatim|Many.usable> and
  <verbatim|Many.crowd2>, including the exact rate inflation and the
  finite-product mechanism. <verbatim|Photo.shade> still consumes the
  selected jet identity, while the source-level support, towing, and push
  helpers require independent mathematical review. The ungrouped response
  receipts in <verbatim|rg-construction.tex> are producer obligations, not
  assumptions discharged by the fiberwise regrouping lemma itself.

  This is a dependency crosswalk, not a claim that the row-level theorem
  alone proves the full continuum statement. The funding curve, top
  polynomial cap, actual tower identity, and public numerical purchases still
  must be supplied by their respective callers. The theorem is conditional on
  exactly these data; it does not produce them by naming a record.

  <section|Proof organization and limits><label|proof-organization-and-limits>

  The terminal packet proof is reorganized from the constant-column
  comparison: the two metric zero modes agree, the strip bounds control both
  saddle packets, and the floor identities give the finite curvature
  representation. For the predecessor step, the local Schur identity and
  neutral-packet push estimate are proved in <verbatim|flat-step.tex>; this
  unit verifies how the actual history supplies its order-two atlas bounds,
  carrier matching, city law, and travel condition. The cost recurrence is
  exact, not an asymptotic convergence argument. Its scalar consequence is
  proved in <verbatim|flat-estimate.tex>.

  No outside result is used to replace a construction estimate: all numerical
  steps here are finite sums, a Schur identity, and the stated scalar
  recurrence. The upstream FlatStep and atlas proofs remain conditional on
  the separate Wilson wire and train estimates audited in the free-kernel
  units. Those source producer chains must still be completed and
  independently reviewed before the full public existence proof is complete.

